  "P15otafat|[P15-otafat] PASS|impl|Validation|B2 OTA DELIVERY — locate the inactive A/B slot inside the SHARED FAT32 boot partition + stage a candidate into its REAL sectors (genuine mkfs.vfat image over virtio-blk): the read-only fat.rs locator parses the MBR → the FAT32 BPB → walks the root directory to HEQK8-B.IMG → follows its cluster chain to a CONTIGUOUS LBA run (fail-closed if fragmented/absent), registers that run as RegionKind::InactiveSlot, and writes a candidate marker through the brick-safety LBA guard (LBA 0 + the active slot + FAT/dir metadata all WriteRefused), read back byte-identical — FAT metadata never mutated (same-size in-place overwrite). QEMU-proven on a real FAT32 fs; the metal eMMC InactiveSlot write arming (emmc.rs clamp) is a separate Gate-R item"
  "P15abcommit|[P15-abcommit] PASS|impl|Validation|B2 A/B COMMIT SURVIVES A COLD BOOT (two boots, one factory-layout disk): the firmware cold-boots config.txt and trial-boots tryboot.txt, so the commit rewrites their kernel= lines in place (equal-length slot names, line inside one sector — no FAT writer) through the guard as BootConfig. Boot 1 commits config.txt -> B and loses power before tryboot.txt; boot 2 reads B back (the commit persisted), detects trial == active and re-points tryboot.txt at A, then a full commit back to A leaves config=A/tryboot=B, and re-committing the active slot writes nothing. Metal: the eMMC Gate-1 clamp must admit the BootConfig sector (Gate R)"
  "Pabslot|[P-abslot] PASS|impl|Validation|Production phase 1 step 3 (OTA brick safety): which boot-partition sectors may an OS-image update write? hal::abslot derives it from the card alone — MBR -> p1 FAT32 BPB -> root directory -> the ONE uncommented kernel=heqk8-[ab].img line in config.txt -> the OTHER slot file, which must be a single contiguous cluster run inside the FAT data area, not overlapping the active slot or the root directory; the eMMC driver uses it as its own Gate 1 (Emmc::admit_inactive_slot — the caller cannot name a range; admitting a boot-config flip revokes it; never the keystore or DataVolume). Proven on the two-boot factory-layout disk on BOTH sides of a commit (config=B -> A's file, config=A -> B's file, each equal to the kernel's independent FAT reader); host tests: legacy single-image line, commented / duplicate lines, fragmented or over-long chains, overlapping slots, missing / duplicate entries, non-FAT32, garbage sweep"
  "P15otaimg|[P15-otaimg] PASS|impl|Validation|Production phase 1 step 4 / ADR 0056 phase 2: OS-image update over the signed-upload channel — the container is the signed boot image itself, staged sector by sector (never whole in RAM); finish runs the SHARED boot verifier over a streamed digest with floor = max(BootInfo floor, running SVN), requires the factory A/B layout (hal::abslot), the image to fit the inactive slot file, the HBoot prefix byte-identical to the installed one (HBoot bytes are not covered by the payload signature, so boot-loader changes stay USB-only), tryboot.txt naming the inactive slot, and the device running its cold-boot slot (never overwrite a running trial's fallback); activate copies Staging into the slot run the storage driver admits on its own and re-hashes the payload FROM THE SLOT, then the AP loop trial-boots it (tryboot one-shot). QEMU single boot on a factory disk with a real-size signed image: accepted -> slot B; refused svn<floor, wrong length, a flipped payload byte, a different HBoot prefix, a running trial; slot A byte-identical after the install; step 5: a boot whose HBoot measurement matches only slot B is classified as its TRIAL, the A/B commit (config=B, tryboot=A, through the store guard) then makes it the cold-boot slot — on metal the AP loop commits only when the AP serves and the WAN is usable, else reboots to the old slot after 5 min"
  "Potagate|[P-otagate] PASS|impl|Validation|release plan WS2 (OTA trust chain): a trial image commits only when the WAN is usable AND the Wi-Fi AP serves (BSS up in AP mode, no firmware halt since boot), both continuously for 30 s — WAN-only or AP-only never commits and reverts after 300 s; a dip restarts the stability window; the limit wins over a late short recovery; only the gate commits (never the watchdog)"
  "AB|[HBoot-AB] PASS|impl|Validation|A/B trial boot: kernel confirms health (hvc #1 disarms HBoot's EL2 watchdog) or firmware falls back to the known-good slot"
  "P7|[P7] PASS|plan|Validation|CM5/RP1 metal bring-up"
)

# HEQK_VALIDATE_FEATX=a,b: extra features for the main QEMU build (e.g. a BENCH-only feature's own gate). Rows that
# only exist with such a feature are added here, so the default run is unchanged.
FEATX="${HEQK_VALIDATE_FEATX:-}"
case ",$FEATX," in
  *,wifiheal-bench,*) PHASES+=("Pwifihealbench|[P-wifiheal-bench] PASS|impl|Validation|BENCH ONLY (feature wifiheal-bench, forbidden in the shipping flavour): the Wi-Fi self-heal metal trigger shapes wifiheal's classifier INPUT (a synthetic persistent TX freeze with the credit window latched, or an injected FWHALT event) and the unchanged ladder acts — freeze-once -> kick 100 ms -> bounce 10 s -> reload 25 s -> cleared; fwhalt -> diagnostics + reload at once; cleared before 10 s -> kicks only; persistent -> reload #2 after the 60-s backoff -> ONE reboot; the boot after it -> Degrade; no probe of the synthetic head; zero heap growth") ;;
esac
case ",$FEATX," in
  *,artstore-bench,*) PHASES+=("Partstorebench|[P-artstore-bench] PASS|impl|Validation|BENCH ONLY (feature artstore-bench, forbidden in the shipping flavour): the ADR 0059 Phase 0.4 metal trigger, msg 41 ARTSTORE_TAMPER_TEST — authorised only by an owner-signed HQMGMT1 envelope bound to the type (none / another operation / another type / replay refused, store untouched); a type with no store entry or with only ONE stored generation refused, nothing written; the accepted trigger flips byte 0 of the ACTIVE half's first data sector (DEVICES gen 8, half B) and nothing else; at the next boot the unchanged loader refuses half B and the real boot_fallback loads the OTHER half (gen 7 in force, its device policy live), not the boot-partition copy") ;;
  *) PHASES+=("Partstorebenchoff|[P-artstore-bench-off] PASS|impl|Validation|default build: msg 41 ARTSTORE_TAMPER_TEST is not compiled in (feature artstore-bench off) — no handler; a validly owner-signed msg-41 envelope drives no compiled-in operation (refused: another operation) and both DEVICES store halves stay byte-identical with gen 8 in force") ;;
esac

echo "==================================================================="
echo " HEQK Core — Kernel Agent Validator (Hardened Edge Quantum-safe Kernel)"
echo "==================================================================="

# --- Stage 1: build -------------------------------------------------------
echo -n "[build] cargo build${FEATX:+ (+$FEATX)} ... "
if ! cargo build --features netsvc,securechannel,securechannel-selftest,wasmhost,wpa3${FEATX:+,$FEATX} >"$BUILD_LOG" 2>&1; then
  echo "FAIL"; echo "  --- build output (last 100 lines) ---"; tail -n 100 "$BUILD_LOG"
  echo "GAP: build broken — cannot validate. Fix compile errors first."; exit 2
fi
echo "ok"

# --- Stage 1b: verifier soundness harness (P16, host-side) ----------------
# Compile the REAL abstract operators (kernel/src/absdom.rs) for the host and
# check each over-approximates the concrete semantics (Agni-style). A control
# injects a deliberately-unsound operator the harness must catch.
echo -n "[P16]   verifier soundness harness ... "
VH="$(mktemp)"
if rustc --edition 2021 -O tools/verifier-harness.rs -o "$VH" >/tmp/hp_vh_build.log 2>&1; then
  if "$VH" >/tmp/hp_vh.log 2>&1; then
    echo "PASS (operators PROVEN SOUND exhaustively over reduced width + sampled on reachable domain; injected unsoundness caught)"
  else
    echo "FAIL — verifier operator UNSOUND:"; sed 's/^/    /' /tmp/hp_vh.log
    rm -f "$VH"; exit 2
  fi
  rm -f "$VH"
else
  echo "skip (rustc host build unavailable)"
fi

# --- Stage 1c: WiFi/WPA crypto KAT harness (P-wifi-crypto, host-side) ------
# aes.rs + wpa.rs are #[cfg(feature="cm5")] so they are ABSENT from the qemu-virt
# kernel — their KATs (aes_selftest/wpa_pmk_selftest) would otherwise never run.
# Compile the REAL source (#[path], no drift) and run FIPS-197 + RFC-3394 wrap/
# unwrap/tamper + PBKDF2 PMK + PTK/MIC self-consistency vectors on the host.
echo -n "[P-wifi-crypto] WiFi/WPA crypto KAT ... "
WCK="$(mktemp)"
if rustc --edition 2021 -O tools/wifi-crypto-kat.rs -o "$WCK" >/tmp/hp_wck_build.log 2>&1; then
  if "$WCK" >/tmp/hp_wck.log 2>&1; then
    echo "PASS (AES-128/RFC3394 wrap+tamper, PBKDF2 PMK, PRF PTK, HMAC-SHA1 MIC)"
  else
    echo "FAIL — WiFi crypto KAT:"; sed 's/^/    /' /tmp/hp_wck.log
    rm -f "$WCK"; exit 2
  fi
  rm -f "$WCK"
else
  echo "skip (rustc host build unavailable)"
fi

# --- Stage 1d: design-doc canon references must resolve --------------------
# Source files, tools and readiness docs cite docs/design/<name>.md as canon. A
# dangling reference (three were found missing on 2026-09-10/11 and reconstructed)
# silently breaks traceability, so fail if any cited design doc is absent.
echo -n "[docs]  design-doc canon refs ... "
DOC_MISSING=0
for d in $(grep -rhoE 'docs/design/heqk-[a-z0-9-]+\.md' --include='*.rs' --include='*.md' --include='*.py' --include='*.sh' . 2>/dev/null | sort -u); do
  if [ ! -f "$d" ]; then echo; echo "  MISSING: $d"; DOC_MISSING=1; fi
done
if [ "$DOC_MISSING" -eq 0 ]; then
  echo "PASS (every cited docs/design/*.md exists)"
else
  echo "FAIL — a cited design doc is missing (dangling canon reference)"; exit 2
fi

# --- Stage 2: boot + capture ---------------------------------------------
# TCG emulation of the PQC self-tests is CPU-bound: the old fixed 45 s budget expired
# mid-boot on a loaded host (load 9 on 4 cores, 2026-10-08) and reported 29 phantom
# phase FAILs. QEMU exits via semihosting as soon as the boot completes, so a larger
# budget costs nothing on a pass — only a genuine hang waits it out.
# 300 s: a healthy boot exits by semihosting long before this, so the limit only bounds a hang; at
# 150 s the self-test-heavy p15-write boots (~100 s each at load 4) timed out under a concurrent build
# and produced phantom FAILs (P15abcommit, Pwasmel0, Pwasip1 — 2026-11-09).
QEMU_TIMEOUT="${HEQK_QEMU_TIMEOUT:-300}"
echo -n "[boot]  qemu virt ... "
timeout "$QEMU_TIMEOUT" $QEMU "$KERNEL" >"$LOG" 2>&1
RC=$?
if grep -q "\[ALL\]" "$LOG"; then echo "clean exit"
elif [ "$RC" = 124 ]; then echo "TIMEOUT after ${QEMU_TIMEOUT}s (load: $(cut -d' ' -f1 /proc/loadavg 2>/dev/null)) — missing markers below may be phantom; rerun on an idle host or raise HEQK_QEMU_TIMEOUT"
  # On GitHub Actions, surface it as an annotation (readable from the public API without the log).
  [ -n "${GITHUB_ACTIONS:-}" ] && echo "::warning title=validate.sh boot timeout::main QEMU boot hit HEQK_QEMU_TIMEOUT=${QEMU_TIMEOUT}s; missing markers may be phantom"
else echo "rc=$RC (no ALL marker; possible hang/regression)"; fi

# --- Stage 2b: M3.1 cross-restart persistence (file-backed virtio-blk) -----
# The volatile RamDisk (P15 above) proves the write-window LOGIC but cannot prove
# "survives reboot". A file-backed virtio-blk device — the SAME hal::BlockDev the
# metal eMMC slots into — can: boot twice against ONE backing file and confirm the
# sealed cookie + data-volume marker persisted. Needs the p15-write build (the
# store WRITE path); the eMMC write driver stays cfg(cm5) = NOT built here.
echo -n "[P15-persist] two-boot persistence (virtio-blk, p15-write) ... "
if command -v dd >/dev/null 2>&1 && cargo build --features netsvc,securechannel,securechannel-selftest,p15-write >/tmp/hp_build_p15w.log 2>&1; then
  DISK="$(mktemp)"; B1="$(mktemp)"; B2="$(mktemp)"
  # Factory step: a 64 MiB image with a valid MBR (p1 FAT @ LBA 2048, 129024
  # sectors). The running kernel is FORBIDDEN to write LBA 0 (brick-safety), so
  # the image tool lays the partition table down — exactly as on a real device.
  dd if=/dev/zero of="$DISK" bs=1M count=64 status=none
  printf '\x0c'             | dd of="$DISK" bs=1 seek=450 conv=notrunc status=none  # part type 0x0c (FAT)
  printf '\x00\x08\x00\x00' | dd of="$DISK" bs=1 seek=454 conv=notrunc status=none  # LBA start = 2048
  printf '\x00\xf8\x01\x00' | dd of="$DISK" bs=1 seek=458 conv=notrunc status=none  # sector count = 129024
  printf '\x55\xaa'         | dd of="$DISK" bs=1 seek=510 conv=notrunc status=none  # 0x55AA boot signature
  QEMU_BLK="qemu-system-aarch64 -M virt -cpu cortex-a72 -m 512M -nographic -serial mon:stdio -semihosting \
    -global virtio-mmio.force-legacy=false -netdev user,id=n0 -device virtio-net-device,netdev=n0 \
    -drive file=$DISK,format=raw,if=none,id=hd0 -device virtio-blk-device,drive=hd0 -kernel"
  # 75s cap (was 45s): the p15-write two-boot now also runs the M4.3 securechannel
  # + enrollment gates, whose debug-mode ML-KEM-768 handshakes add real wall time.
  timeout "$QEMU_TIMEOUT" $QEMU_BLK "$KERNEL" >"$B1" 2>&1   # boot 1: write cookie+marker through the guard
  timeout "$QEMU_TIMEOUT" $QEMU_BLK "$KERNEL" >"$B2" 2>&1   # boot 2: SAME disk -> read back + unseal
  cat "$B1" "$B2" >> "$LOG"                     # feed both boots' markers into the report
  if grep -qF "[P15-persist] PASS" "$B2"; then
    echo "PASS (cookie+marker survived restart)"
  else
    echo "FAIL/see report"; echo "  --- boot1 tail ---"; grep -F "[P15-persist]" "$B1" | sed 's/^/    /'
    echo "  --- boot2 tail ---"; grep -F "[P15-persist]" "$B2" | sed 's/^/    /'
  fi
  rm -f "$DISK" "$B1" "$B2"
else
  echo "skip (no dd, or p15-write build failed — see /tmp/hp_build_p15w.log)"
fi

# --- Stage 2c: B2 (M3.4) OTA DELIVERY — locate the inactive A/B slot inside the
# SHARED FAT32 boot partition and stage a candidate into its REAL sectors. Builds a
# genuine mkfs.vfat FAT32 image (heqk8.img + heqk8-b.img copied in), boots heqk against
# it as virtio-blk, and the kernel parses the BPB + walks the root dir + follows the
# cluster chain to HEQK8-B.IMG, registers that run as InactiveSlot, and writes a
# candidate through the brick-safety guard. Needs the p15-write kernel from Stage 2b.
echo -n "[P15-otafat] FAT32 locate + guarded slot-B candidate write ... "
if command -v mkfs.vfat >/dev/null 2>&1 && command -v mcopy >/dev/null 2>&1 \
   && command -v dd >/dev/null 2>&1 && [ -f "$KERNEL" ]; then
  FATDISK="$(mktemp)"; PART="$(mktemp)"; CAND="$(mktemp)"; BO="$(mktemp)"
  # A 63 MiB FAT32 partition image (>= FAT32 min clusters), 512-B clusters.
  dd if=/dev/zero of="$PART" bs=512 count=129024 status=none
  mkfs.vfat -F 32 -s 1 "$PART" >/dev/null 2>&1
  # A 256 KiB candidate; copy it as BOTH slots (fresh FS => each contiguous). HEQK8-B.IMG
  # is the INACTIVE target the kernel must locate; HEQK8.IMG is the active slot (never written).
  dd if=/dev/urandom of="$CAND" bs=1K count=256 status=none
  mcopy -i "$PART" "$CAND" ::HEQK8.IMG   >/dev/null 2>&1
  mcopy -i "$PART" "$CAND" ::HEQK8-B.IMG >/dev/null 2>&1
  # A 64 MiB disk with an MBR: FAT partition @ LBA 2048 (129024 sectors); the running
  # kernel is FORBIDDEN LBA 0, so the tool lays the table + copies the FS in (as on metal).
  dd if=/dev/zero of="$FATDISK" bs=1M count=64 status=none
  printf '\x0c'             | dd of="$FATDISK" bs=1 seek=450 conv=notrunc status=none  # type 0x0c (FAT)
  printf '\x00\x08\x00\x00' | dd of="$FATDISK" bs=1 seek=454 conv=notrunc status=none  # LBA start 2048
  printf '\x00\xf8\x01\x00' | dd of="$FATDISK" bs=1 seek=458 conv=notrunc status=none  # count 129024
  printf '\x55\xaa'         | dd of="$FATDISK" bs=1 seek=510 conv=notrunc status=none  # 0x55AA sig
  dd if="$PART" of="$FATDISK" bs=512 seek=2048 conv=notrunc status=none
  QEMU_FAT="qemu-system-aarch64 -M virt -cpu cortex-a72 -m 512M -nographic -serial mon:stdio -semihosting \
    -global virtio-mmio.force-legacy=false -netdev user,id=n0 -device virtio-net-device,netdev=n0 \
    -drive file=$FATDISK,format=raw,if=none,id=hd0 -device virtio-blk-device,drive=hd0 -kernel"
  timeout "$QEMU_TIMEOUT" $QEMU_FAT "$KERNEL" >"$BO" 2>&1
  cat "$BO" >> "$LOG"
  if grep -qF "[P15-otafat] PASS" "$BO"; then
    echo "PASS (located HEQK8-B.IMG in FAT32 + staged candidate through the guard)"
  else
    echo "FAIL/see report"; grep -F "[P15-otafat]" "$BO" | sed 's/^/    /'
  fi
  rm -f "$FATDISK" "$PART" "$CAND" "$BO"
else
  echo "skip (no mkfs.vfat/mcopy/dd, or no p15-write kernel)"
fi

# --- Stage 2d: B2 A/B COMMIT survives a cold boot — TWO boots on ONE factory-layout disk.
# config.txt/tryboot.txt are generated exactly like os/build/make-cm5-heqk-disk.sh (slot names of
# equal length, the kernel= line inside one sector). Boot 1 commits to B but writes only
# config.txt (simulated power loss); boot 2 must find B persisted, repair tryboot.txt, then do a
# full commit back to A. Needs the p15-write kernel from Stage 2b.
echo -n "[P15-abcommit] A/B commit across a reboot + interrupted-commit repair ... "
if command -v mkfs.vfat >/dev/null 2>&1 && command -v mcopy >/dev/null 2>&1 && [ -f "$KERNEL" ]; then
  ABDISK="$(mktemp)"; ABPART="$(mktemp)"; ABW="$(mktemp -d)"; AB1="$(mktemp)"; AB2="$(mktemp)"
  dd if=/dev/zero of="$ABPART" bs=512 count=129024 status=none
  mkfs.vfat -F 32 -s 1 "$ABPART" >/dev/null 2>&1
  python3 -I - "$ABW" cm5-boot/config-nolinux.txt <<'PY'
import sys, re
out, tpl = sys.argv[1], sys.argv[2]
lines = [l for l in open(tpl).read().splitlines() if not re.match(r'\s*kernel\s*=', l)]
for name, slot in (("config.txt", "a"), ("tryboot.txt", "b")):
    body = ["# heqk A/B boot config (validate.sh, factory format)"] + lines
    head = ("\n".join(body) + "\n").encode(); line = f"kernel=heqk8-{slot}.img"
    if len(head) % 512 + len(line) > 512:
        body.append("#" * max(512 - len(head) % 512 - 1, 1))
    open(f"{out}/{name}", "w").write("\n".join(body + [line, ""]))
PY
  dd if=/dev/urandom of="$ABW/slot" bs=1K count=64 status=none
  for f in config.txt tryboot.txt; do mcopy -i "$ABPART" "$ABW/$f" ::"$f" >/dev/null 2>&1; done
  mcopy -i "$ABPART" "$ABW/slot" ::HEQK8-A.IMG >/dev/null 2>&1
  mcopy -i "$ABPART" "$ABW/slot" ::HEQK8-B.IMG >/dev/null 2>&1
  dd if=/dev/zero of="$ABDISK" bs=1M count=64 status=none
  printf 'start=2048, size=129024, type=c\n' | sfdisk --quiet --label dos "$ABDISK" 2>/dev/null
  dd if="$ABPART" of="$ABDISK" bs=512 seek=2048 conv=notrunc status=none
  QEMU_AB="qemu-system-aarch64 -M virt -cpu cortex-a72 -m 512M -nographic -serial mon:stdio -semihosting \
    -global virtio-mmio.force-legacy=false -netdev user,id=n0 -device virtio-net-device,netdev=n0 \
    -drive file=$ABDISK,format=raw,if=none,id=hd0 -device virtio-blk-device,drive=hd0 -kernel"
  timeout "$QEMU_TIMEOUT" $QEMU_AB "$KERNEL" >"$AB1" 2>&1   # boot 1: commit config only (crash)
  timeout "$QEMU_TIMEOUT" $QEMU_AB "$KERNEL" >"$AB2" 2>&1   # boot 2: same disk -> repair + full commit
  cat "$AB1" "$AB2" >> "$LOG"
  if grep -qF "[P15-abcommit] boot 1: committed" "$AB1" && grep -qF "[P15-abcommit] PASS" "$AB2"; then
    echo "PASS (commit persisted across the reboot; interrupted commit repaired; full commit + idempotent)"
  else
    echo "FAIL/see report"; grep -hF "[P15-abcommit]" "$AB1" "$AB2" | sed 's/^/    /'
  fi
  rm -rf "$ABDISK" "$ABPART" "$ABW" "$AB1" "$AB2"
else
  echo "skip (no mkfs.vfat/mcopy, or no p15-write kernel)"
fi

# --- P15-otaimg: OS-image update over the upload path (production phase 1) ----
# A factory-layout disk whose slot A holds a REAL-SIZE signed image (HBoot-prefix pattern + the dev-
# signed 3,000,000-byte-zero-body header fixture + the body) and slot B junk of the same size;
# config=A, tryboot=B. One boot: stage, check (+ refusals), install into B, re-hash from the slot.
echo -n "[P15-otaimg] OS-image update: stage -> verify -> inactive slot ... "
if command -v mkfs.vfat >/dev/null 2>&1 && command -v mcopy >/dev/null 2>&1 && [ -f "$KERNEL" ]; then
  OD="$(mktemp)"; OP="$(mktemp)"; OW="$(mktemp -d)"; OL="$(mktemp)"
  python3 -I - "$OW" kernel/src/testdata/ota_big_hdr.bin <<'PY'
import sys, random
out, hdr = sys.argv[1], open(sys.argv[2], 'rb').read()
r = random.Random(7)
pre = bytes(r.getrandbits(8) for _ in range(0x200000))
open(f"{out}/a", "wb").write(pre + hdr + bytes(3000000))
open(f"{out}/b", "wb").write(bytes(r.getrandbits(8) for _ in range(0x200000 + len(hdr) + 3000000)))
for name, slot in (("config.txt", "a"), ("tryboot.txt", "b")):
    open(f"{out}/{name}", "w").write(f"# heqk A/B boot config (validate.sh OTA disk)\narm_64bit=1\nkernel=heqk8-{slot}.img\n")
PY
  dd if=/dev/zero of="$OP" bs=512 count=131072 status=none
  mkfs.vfat -F 32 -s 8 "$OP" >/dev/null 2>&1
  for f in config.txt tryboot.txt; do mcopy -i "$OP" "$OW/$f" ::"$f" >/dev/null 2>&1; done
  mcopy -i "$OP" "$OW/a" ::heqk8-a.img >/dev/null 2>&1
  mcopy -i "$OP" "$OW/b" ::heqk8-b.img >/dev/null 2>&1
  # p1 at LBA 32768: earlier p15 self-tests in the same boot write scratch sectors at fixed LBAs
  # (around 8192, the real factory p1 start) — keep the OTA slots clear of them.
  dd if=/dev/zero of="$OD" bs=1M count=96 status=none
  printf 'start=32768, size=131072, type=c\n' | sfdisk --quiet --label dos "$OD" 2>/dev/null
  dd if="$OP" of="$OD" bs=512 seek=32768 conv=notrunc status=none
  timeout "$QEMU_TIMEOUT" qemu-system-aarch64 -M virt -cpu cortex-a72 -m 512M -nographic -serial mon:stdio -semihosting \
    -global virtio-mmio.force-legacy=false -netdev user,id=n0 -device virtio-net-device,netdev=n0 \
    -drive file="$OD",format=raw,if=none,id=hd0 -device virtio-blk-device,drive=hd0 -kernel "$KERNEL" >"$OL" 2>&1
  cat "$OL" >> "$LOG"
  if grep -qF "[P15-otaimg] PASS" "$OL"; then echo "PASS"; else echo "FAIL/see report"; grep -aF "[P15-otaimg]" "$OL" | sed 's/^/    /'; fi
  rm -rf "$OD" "$OP" "$OW" "$OL"
else
  echo "skip (no mkfs.vfat/mcopy, or no p15-write kernel)"
fi

# --- Stage 3: phase gate report ------------------------------------------
printf "\n %-4s %-8s %-30s %s\n" "PH" "STATUS" "LIFECYCLE STAGE" "GATE"
printf " %-4s %-8s %-30s %s\n" "----" "------" "------------------------------" "----------------------------------------"
FAILS=0; GAPS=0; FIRST_FAIL=""; FAILED_LIST=()
for row in "${PHASES[@]}"; do
  IFS='|' read -r ph marker kind stage what <<< "$row"
  if grep -qF "$marker" "$LOG"; then
    st="PASS"
  elif [ "$kind" = "plan" ]; then
    st="PLANNED"; GAPS=$((GAPS+1))
  else
    st="FAIL"; FAILS=$((FAILS+1)); FAILED_LIST+=("$ph")
    [ -z "$FIRST_FAIL" ] && FIRST_FAIL="$ph|$marker|$what"
  fi
  printf " %-4s %-8s %-30s %s\n" "$ph" "$st" "$stage" "$what"
done

# --- Stage 4: verdict + auto-diagnostics (heal fast) ----------------------
echo ""
echo " built phases failing : $FAILS"
echo " gaps (not yet built) : $GAPS   (next: first PLANNED phase above)"
if [ "$FAILS" -gt 0 ]; then
  IFS='|' read -r ff_ph ff_marker ff_what <<< "$FIRST_FAIL"
  echo ""
  echo " ┌─ HEAL: first failing gate = $ff_ph ($ff_what)"
  echo " │  missing marker: '$ff_marker'"
  # GitHub Actions annotation: names every failing gate without needing the (auth-only) log.
  if [ -n "${GITHUB_ACTIONS:-}" ]; then
    echo "::error title=validate.sh: ${FAILS} failing gate(s)::first = ${ff_ph}, missing '${ff_marker}'. Failing: $(printf '%s ' "${FAILED_LIST[@]:-}")"
  fi
  if grep -qE 'EXCEPTION|PANIC' "$LOG"; then
    echo " │  fault detected — dumping the exception/panic:"
    grep -E 'EXCEPTION|PANIC|ESR_EL1|ELR_EL1|FAR_EL1' "$LOG" | sed 's/^/ │    /'
  elif ! grep -q "\[ALL\]" "$LOG"; then
    echo " │  no clean exit (hang or early abort) — last 12 console lines:"
    grep -v '^\s*$' "$LOG" | tail -12 | sed 's/^/ │    /'
  fi
  echo " └─ next: the kernel-validator agent diagnoses at $ff_ph's code and re-runs ./validate.sh"
  [ -n "${VALIDATE_KEEP_LOG:-}" ] || rm -f "$LOG"
  echo " VERDICT: REGRESSION — heal required (diagnostics above)."
  exit 1
fi
[ -n "${VALIDATE_KEEP_LOG:-}" ] || rm -f "$LOG"
echo " VERDICT: all implemented phases GREEN. Kernel is healthy."
echo " (continuous V&V + runtime self-heal (P6b); see LIFECYCLE.md + the kernel-validator agent.)"
exit 0
